{#
  T-2.07 — the verification-code field.

  Usage:
    {% include 'components.ui.otp' with { id: 'otp', label: trans('…'), length: 4 } only %}

  Parameters:
    id       required — prefixes each segment's id
    label    required — names the group
    length   number of digits, default 4 (the artboard's)
    error    optional — a message, announced

  FOUR INPUTS, NOT ONE. `Verification Code Bottom Sheet Step 3.svg` draws four
  boxes, each `≈85×47 rx11.5`, the focused one bordered darker. A single input
  styled to look like four cannot put the caret in the third box; four inputs
  can, and each is a real field a screen reader can name.

  THE ROW IS `dir="ltr"` AND ITS LABEL IS NOT. A verification code reads
  left-to-right in every language, and the artboard draws the first digit at the
  left of an otherwise right-to-left page. **This is not the case T-1.04 warns
  about:** that warning is against putting isolation on a block that also holds
  RTL text, where it re-resolves the block's own `text-align: start`. This row
  holds four digits and nothing else, and the label sits outside it.

  `autocomplete="one-time-code"` GOES ON THE FIRST SEGMENT ONLY. The browser
  fills that one and the paste handler below distributes the rest — putting the
  token on all four makes several browsers fill every box with the whole code.

  EACH SEGMENT IS NAMED BY POSITION. "Digit 3 of 4" is what a screen-reader user
  needs to know when focus jumps on its own, and focus jumping on its own is the
  whole behaviour of this control.
#}
{% set otp_length = length|default(4) %}
{% set otp_error = error is defined and error is not empty %}

<div class="field otp {{ otp_error ? 'field--invalid' : '' }}">
    <span class="field__label" id="{{ id }}-label">{{ label }}</span>

    <div class="otp__row"
         role="group"
         dir="ltr"
         aria-labelledby="{{ id }}-label"
         data-otp
         {% if otp_error %}aria-describedby="{{ id }}-error"{% endif %}>
        {% for i in 1..otp_length %}
            <input class="field__input otp__digit"
                   id="{{ id }}-{{ i }}"
                   type="text"
                   inputmode="numeric"
                   pattern="[0-9]*"
                   maxlength="1"
                   data-otp-digit
                   {% if i == 1 %}autocomplete="one-time-code"{% else %}autocomplete="off"{% endif %}
                   {% if otp_error %}aria-invalid="true"{% endif %}
                   aria-label="{{ trans('theme.form.otp_digit', { position: i, total: otp_length }) }}">
        {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {% if otp_error %}
        <p class="field__error" id="{{ id }}-error" role="alert">
            {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'cancel-circle' } only %}
            {{ error }}
        </p>
    {% endif %}
</div>
